Suppose for contradiction that the conclusion of this theorem does not hold. Then there exist a positive sequence $\{\zeta_k\}$, a sequence $\{z^k\} \subset \cS$, and some $j \in \{1,...,m\}$ such that $\lim_{k\to\infty }\zeta_k = 0$ and  
\beq \label{bc-ineq1}
 \bc_{j}(y, z^k) > -\zeta_k \quad  \forall y\in\cY, \, \forall k.
